Even a clear fit had to type his answer, and typing is where answers die.

- Migration 219: task_asks.prepared_answer.
- On a first ask whose pre-match (1694) is likely_yes, one line is composed
  by the editor model with the brief Misho approved tonight, word for word
  (§107), from the reader's own profile fields only (job, employer,
  user_profile_kv) — never his notes, never anything he typed. A line with a
  number, two lines, or over 200 characters is not used.
- It is stored on the ask and shown only to him, under the question:
  „„კი, ვიცნობ"-ს დაჭერით გაიგზავნება: „…"".
- His tap on „yes" sends exactly that line as his answer, by the server
  (worded at send as every answer, D652); he reads „გაიგზავნა: „…"". no and
  later behave as today; nothing is sent without the tap.

NOT IN THIS COMMIT: „other" opening the box pre-filled with the line needs
the frontend; the contract follows in FOR_FRONTEND.md.

DONE WHEN: the likely_yes seat of A11 sees a one-line prepared answer under
yes; a tap sends it and the asker receives it with the facts exact; the
asker never sees the line before the tap; a seat on possibly / ask_him sees
no line.

